  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#editors\r\n\r\n> For example, it is not conforming to use an address element for arbitrary contact information; that element can only be used for marking up contact information for the author of the document or section\\.\r\n\r\nDoes this actually mean \"... for the author of the document or article\", since the semantics defined for [address][addr] is:\r\n\r\n> The address element represents the contact information for its nearest article or body element ancestor. If that is the body element, then the contact information applies to the document as a whole.\r\n\r\n[addr]: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#the-address-element",
